# RIL Linkage Map Construction and QTL Analysis

**Complete supplied commands and R code for SNP binning, linkage-map evaluation and composite interval mapping in a cucumber recombinant inbred line population.**

## Overview

| Stage | Software | Main result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Infer genotype crosspoints | SNPbinner | Crosspoint calls for each RIL |
| Construct bin markers | SNPbinner | Per-chromosome bin genotypes |
| Convert genotype formats | Custom R/Python scripts | Lep-MAP3 input |
| Evaluate the input marker order | Lep-MAP3 | Per-chromosome genetic maps |
| Fill genotypes and re-estimate distances | R/qtl | Updated map and cross data |
| Composite interval mapping (CIM) | R/qtl | Trait-specific LOD profiles |
| Permutation testing and peak processing | R/qtl and custom peak function | Thresholds and candidate QTL summaries |

The Bash block below preserves the supplied analysis parameters, with quoting and line wrapping for readability. The full R block reproduces the uploaded QTL script unchanged, including its original comments and project-specific paths. Review the implementation notes at the end before reuse.

## 1. Requirements and input files

| Requirement | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| SNPbinner | `snpbinner crosspoints` and `snpbinner bins` |
| Java and Lep-MAP3 | `ParentCall2` and `OrderMarkers2` |
| R | Packages `qtl`, `eqtl` and `parallel` loaded by the supplied script |
| `SNP.Code.chr1.tsv` … `SNP.Code.chr7.tsv` | SNP genotype tables, ordered by chromosome position |
| `Convert.Format.bin2hp.R` | Custom bin-format conversion script |
| `hp2lepmap.py` | Custom converter invoked once per chromosome |
| `pedigree.txt` | Pedigree matching the genotype samples and Lep-MAP3 encoding |
| `chr1_7.qtl.xls` | Combined genotype/map file in R/qtl `csvs` format |
| `Input.Traits.csv` | Phenotype file in the corresponding R/qtl format |
| `define.peak.R` | Custom file defining `define.peak1()` |

The custom converters, pedigree, combined R/qtl input and peak-definition function were not supplied. In particular, the code that combines the chromosome maps into `chr1_7.qtl.xls` is not present, so that file must be prepared separately. Its `.xls` extension does not make it an Excel workbook: `read.cross("csvs", ...)` expects the R/qtl text format.

For SNPbinner, the input includes a marker identifier, physical position and RIL genotype columns. Retain consistent individual identifiers and genotype encodings through all conversions. Keep physical positions in bp and linkage positions in cM distinguishable.

## 2. Linkage map construction: complete Bash commands

Save this block as `build_RIL_linkage_map.sh` and run it from the directory containing the SNP tables, converter R script and pedigree:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash

for i in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
do
    snpbinner crosspoints \
        --input "SNP.Code.chr${i}.tsv" \
        --output "SNP.Code.chr${i}.cross.out" \
        --min-ratio 0.01

    snpbinner bins \
        --input "SNP.Code.chr${i}.cross.out" \
        --output "SNP.Code.chr${i}.bin.out" \
        --min-bin-size 5000

    Rscript Convert.Format.bin2hp.R "SNP.Code.chr${i}.bin.out"

    /home/GuanJianTao/Low.Temperature.Experiments.dir/Binmap.dir/create.binmap.dir/hp2lepmap.py \
        "$i"

    java -Xmx50g \
        -cp /home/GuanJianTao/Software/Lep_Map3/bin \
        ParentCall2 \
        data=pedigree.txt \
        posteriorFile="chr${i}.for_lepmap" \
        removeNonInformative=1 \
        > "chr${i}.call.xls"

    awk '{if($1!~/CHR/ && $1!~/^#/){print 1}}' \
        "chr${i}.call.xls" > "chr${i}.group"

    awk '{if($1!~/CHR/ && $1!~/^#/){n=n+1;print n}}' \
        "chr${i}.call.xls" > "chr${i}.fix_order.txt"

    java -Xmx100g \
        -cp /home/GuanJianTao/Software/Lep_Map3/bin \
        OrderMarkers2 \
        data="chr${i}.call.xls" \
        map="chr${i}.group" \
        identicalLimit=0.01 \
        minError=0.001 \
        sexAveraged=1 \
        informativeMask=3 \
        numThreads=20 \
        recombination1=0.001 \
        recombination2=0.001 \
        interference1=0.01 \
        interference2=0.01 \
        phasedData=0 \
        evaluateOrder="chr${i}.fix_order.txt" \
        improveOrder=0 \
        useKosambi=1 \
        grandparentPhase=1 \
        computeLODScores="chr${i}.lod.xls" \
        selfingPhase=1 \
        > "chr${i}.lepmap.xls"
done
```

Run with:

```bash
bash build_RIL_linkage_map.sh
```

### Key settings and interpretation

| Setting | Value | Interpretation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Crosspoint `--min-ratio` | `0.01` | Minimum crosspoint spacing as a fraction of chromosome length; 1% here |
| Binning `--min-bin-size` | `5000` | Requested minimum bin size, in bp |
| `removeNonInformative` | `1` | Remove noninformative markers during parent calling |
| Group assignment | All retained rows assigned `1` within each chromosome run | Chromosome membership is supplied rather than inferred here |
| `evaluateOrder` | Sequential marker indices | Evaluate the existing input order |
| `improveOrder` | `0` | Retain that order |
| `sexAveraged` | `1` | Request a sex-averaged map |
| `useKosambi` | `1` | Use the Kosambi mapping function |
| `numThreads` | `20` | Threads requested for OrderMarkers2 |
| Java heap | `50g` / `100g` | Maximum heap allocation for the two Java steps |

The fixed order is a physical order only if all preceding input and conversion steps preserve physical ordering. This implementation does not independently infer seven linkage groups or freely reorder markers. Also, SNPbinner infers chromosome length from the last SNP when `--chrom-len` is not provided; the 1% spacing threshold can therefore depend on marker coverage.

